[{"id":"wait-predict-start","itemId":"readiness-count","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 11.4's <code class=\"nobreak\">layer_wait</code> with N = 8, T = 3 and R = 1: three taps a position, and position p reads up to p + 1. The producer writes a position every four cycles, and <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> counts them; <code class=\"nobreak\">np</code> is the position whose taps come next. <code class=\"nobreak\">run</code> is 1 in the cycle after an edge that issued a tap. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">run</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>Position 0 reads up to position 1, so it needs <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> to be more than 1. <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> becomes 2 halfway through cycle 1, so the edges that start cycles 2, 3 and 4 issue its three taps. Position 1 needs <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> above 2: it comes halfway through cycle 5, so the edge of cycle 5 issues nothing, and cycles 6 to 8 get position 1's taps. Position 2 waits in cycle 9 for <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> to reach 4 the same way.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"wait-start","source":"hdl/level-11/layer_wait/layer_wait_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":10,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"layer_wait_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"]]},{"label":"wr[3:0]","path":"layer_wait_tb.wr","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0001"],[1.5,"0010"],[5.5,"0011"],[9.5,"0100"]]},{"label":"np[3:0]","path":"layer_wait_tb.dut.np","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[4,"0001"],[8,"0010"]]},{"label":"run","path":"layer_wait_tb.run","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[9,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","1","1","1","0","1","1","1","0"]}]},"answer":"run","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"wait-predict-stall","itemId":"readiness-count","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 11.4's <code class=\"nobreak\">layer_wait</code> with N = 8, T = 3 and R = 1, reset in cycle 0: three taps a position, and position p reads up to p + 1. <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> counts the producer's writes, which come unevenly; <code class=\"nobreak\">np</code> is not drawn. <code class=\"nobreak\">run</code> is 1 in the cycle after an edge that issued a tap. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">run</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>Each position's first tap needs <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> above p + 1 at its edge, and the next two taps follow without a check. Position 0 starts in cycle 2, once <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> is 2. Position 1 needs 3, which comes halfway through cycle 5: cycle 5 is empty, taps in 6 to 8. Position 2 needs 4, halfway through cycle 10: cycles 9 and 10 are empty, taps in 11 to 13. Position 3 needs 5, which came in cycle 12, so it starts at once in cycle 14.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"wait-stall","source":"hdl/level-11/layer_wait/layer_wait_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":15,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"layer_wait_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"],[10,"1"],[10.5,"0"],[11,"1"],[11.5,"0"],[12,"1"],[12.5,"0"],[13,"1"],[13.5,"0"],[14,"1"],[14.5,"0"]]},{"label":"rst","path":"layer_wait_tb.rst","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"]]},{"label":"wr[3:0]","path":"layer_wait_tb.wr","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[0.5,"0001"],[1.5,"0010"],[5.5,"0011"],[10.5,"0100"],[12.5,"0101"],[14.5,"0110"]]},{"label":"run","path":"layer_wait_tb.run","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[9,"0"],[11,"1"]],"samples":["0","0","1","1","1","0","1","1","1","0","0","1","1","1","1"]}]},"answer":"run"},{"id":"wait-find-bug","itemId":"readiness-count","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">layer_wait_bug</code> should issue every tap of all eight positions, as lesson 11.4's <code class=\"nobreak\">layer_wait</code> does. Its testbench fails at the last position: the producer has written all 8, and the layer never starts position 7. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>Position 7 reads up to position 8, which is past the end of the map: nobody ever writes it, so <code class=\"nobreak\">wr</code> never gets above 8. A layer may also start once the producer has written all N positions, <code>wr == 4'(N)</code>. Without that, the last position waits for ever, and so does every layer after it.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-11/layer_wait_bug/layer_wait_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// The sequencer of a layer that waits for the layer before it, as each","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// layer of the decoder does. The layer works through positions 0 to","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// N - 1, one tap a cycle, T taps a position. Position p reads the","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// producer's positions up to p + R, and the producer writes its","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// positions in order, counting them in wr. So position p may start only","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// when wr is more than p + R, or when the producer has written all N","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// positions: past the end there is nothing to wait for. Until then the","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// layer freezes and issues nothing: run is 0 for that cycle, an empty","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// slot. Once a position starts, its T taps follow without a pause.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"layer_wait_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"#","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"int","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" N ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"8","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":",             ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// positions in the map","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"int","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" T ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":",             ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// taps a position, one a cycle","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"int","color":"var(